file C:\MIRC\#oddbuilds.log
	icon: res://win95/theme/icons/document_text_32.png
	contents:
		[22:58] *** Now talking in #oddbuilds
		[22:58] *** Topic is 'post your build numbers. no warez.'
		[23:01] <elmroot> anyone else seen 4.06.6612?
		[23:01] <tarnhelm> 4.00.950 here. 4.00.1111 if you know someone at an OEM
		[23:02] <elmroot> 4.06. System Properties says so. Microsoft never made a 4.06
		[23:02] <tarnhelm> someone edited the registry for a joke
		[23:03] <elmroot> three machines now, three towns. none of the owners remember installing it
		[23:04] <quill> a guy brought one in at work. said a friend gave him floppies
		[23:04] <quill> 13 disks, labelled by hand, no hologram
		[23:05] <elmroot> what did the labels say
		[23:05] <quill> "update" and a number
		[23:06] <tarnhelm> so it's a pirate copy with a fake version
		[23:07] <elmroot> pirates don't invent build numbers. and setup is 1.4 megs bigger than retail
		[23:08] <quill> what's in the extra 1.4
		[23:08] <elmroot> working on it
		[23:12] *** tarnhelm has quit IRC (Leaving)
		
		[01:14] *** Now talking in #oddbuilds
		[01:15] <quill> elmroot. the 6612 guy came back. his calculator says 666
		[01:15] <elmroot> for what sum
		[01:15] <quill> any sum. 2+2. 666
		[01:16] <quill> calc on a normal build is fine. same size. different date
		[01:17] <elmroot> don't copy anything off it. don't put your own disks in it
		[01:17] <quill> too late. i copied calc.exe to look at it
		[01:18] <elmroot> then throw that floppy away
		[01:19] <quill> you sound like my mom
		[01:20] <elmroot> i mean it
		
	contents_file: res://customers/activist_guy/mirc_logs/oddbuilds.log
	modified: Thursday, May 30, 1996 1:20:41 AM

file C:\MIRC\fl0ppyjoe.log
	icon: res://win95/theme/icons/document_text_32.png
	contents:
		[20:31] <fl0ppyjoe> u the guy asking about the 4.06 disks?
		[20:31] <elmroot> yes. where did yours come from
		[20:32] <fl0ppyjoe> swap meet at the community center. guy had a box of them. 5 bucks a set
		[20:32] <elmroot> what did he look like
		[20:33] <fl0ppyjoe> didnt look. there was a line
		[20:33] <fl0ppyjoe> sold out in an hour. everyone wanted the new windows
		[20:34] <elmroot> do you still have the set?
		[20:35] <fl0ppyjoe> gave it to my cousin. he copied it for half his school
		[20:35] <elmroot> how many copies
		[20:36] <fl0ppyjoe> dunno. lots. why
		[20:37] <elmroot> because it copies itself too
		[20:38] <fl0ppyjoe> lol ok mulder
		
	contents_file: res://customers/activist_guy/mirc_logs/fl0ppyjoe.log
	modified: Sunday, May 12, 1996 8:38:12 PM

